@@ -81,13 +81,12 @@ https://github.com/oriansj/talk-notes/blob/master/bootstrappable.org
 
 ## How does this process work?
 
-It is highly recommended that after reading this you go through the kaem.run for
-your architecture and see each of these steps in action. Note that the kaem.run
-is split into two kaem files to make it simpler to grasp. These two files are
-mescc-tools-mini-kaem.kaem for Phase 0-9 (uses the simple kaem),
-mescc-tools-full-kaem.kaem for Phase 10-12 (uses the full kaem for the rest of
-mescc-tools) and mes-m2.kaem for Phase 13, contained in the same folder as
-kaem.run.
+Start with kaem.<architecture>: seed/minimal kaem builds the initial tools
+and bake in mescc-tools-mini-kaem.kaem. The architecture's bootstrap.*.bake
+then supplies machine parameters to bootstrap.common.bake. The shared
+mescc-tools-full.bake rebuilds the full tools before the extra tools and
+checksum verification. No full kaem interpreter or duplicated full-tool
+rebuild scripts are needed.
 
 ALL of these steps have a NASM or GAS version in the NASM/ or GAS/ subdirectory
 of the folder for the architecture.
@@ -187,10 +186,11 @@ features provided by M2libc and M2-Planet to enable significantly faster builds.
 This is the final debuggable version of hex2 with all of the optimizations and
 features provided by M2libc and M2-Planet to enable significantly faster builds.
 
-### Phase 11: Build kaem
+### Phase 11: Build bake
 
-kaem is what was being used to run kaem.run scripts, and is useful for
-later stages of the bootstrap process outside this repository.
+The seed-built compiler builds bake, which runs named targets and dependencies
+for the rest of the bootstrap. The minimal kaem seed is still required for the
+initial steps; the full kaem interpreter is replaced.
 
 ### Phase 12: Build blood-elf implementation in M2-Planet
 
@@ -271,9 +271,8 @@ supported) and replaces it with the desired replacement.
 If you need a chroot or to isolate what you are doing; wrap is the first tool
 available for that job and does it well enough to get you quite far.
 
-### Phase 28: after.kaem
+### Phase 28: after.bake
 
-after.kaem exists for you to replace with anything you want to kick off your
-bootstrap chain.
+after.bake provides the `all` target for continuing your bootstrap chain.
 
 Enjoy
